{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794334387,"nonce":"nFdw89zlknRw3N0z6hv9vkKG0M4=","title":"Documentation fails on main: the component previews were recorded before the shared styles changed","message":"The Build Book step runs the catalog tool, which rejects a recording whose fixture digest no longer matches. The digest covers crates/blinc_cn/src/cn_styles.rs, crates/blinc_layout/src/ua_styles.rs and the demo sources, all of which changed on main after the previews were last recorded, so every component's recording was stale (the error names the first one, button: \"catalog: button recording is stale; regenerate with --record\"). Documentation has failed on main since 2ca5f509 and on the open PR branched from it.\n\nFix: re-record with cargo run -p blinc-build-web-examples -- --catalog-to \u003cdir\u003e --record and commit web/components/previews. Whenever cn_styles.rs, ua_styles.rs or the demo sources change, the previews have to be re-recorded in the same push; the CI list for a push should include the catalog check (cargo run -p blinc-build-web-examples -- --catalog-to \u003cdir\u003e, which fails on a stale recording before it reaches the wasm bundle).\n\nThe recordings re-made after the russl SDF port match the ones made before it: 76 of 82 components are byte-identical, and the other six (accordion, collapsible, notch, tabs, audio-player, video-player) vary between runs of the same commit by as much as between commits. All 184 snapshot images the blinc_recorder tests render are bit-identical before and after.","files":null}]}